# Plant-language naming (full surface — pay once)

Before the first migration **and** the first feature package / API:

1. Lock the **plant noun** operators/quality use (e.g. Panel Registration, process path, work order).
2. Align the **whole surface** to that noun — or keep names recognizably close. Do not invent a parallel vocab (ERP “management”, vague “data”, demo placeholders).

| Layer | Prefer aligned / close | Avoid |
|-------|------------------------|--------|
| Story / ticket / docs | Panel Registration | WO management, data entry |
| Package / feature folder | `panelregistration` | `womanagement`, `datamgmt` |
| API path + resource | `/api/panel-registrations` | `/api/wo-management` |
| Request / response / service | `PanelRegistration*` | `WoManagement*` |
| Table + columns | `panel_registration`, `panel_number`, … | `wo_management`, vague `mgmt_*` |
| JPA entity `@Table` | matches table / plant noun | entity plant-ish, table ERP-ish (drift) |

**Rule of thumb:** a plant PM reading the URL, class name, or table name should recognize the same process. Slight abbreviation (`panelregistration` package) is fine; **far-away** names are not.

**Historical note:** `wo_management` was renamed to `panel_registration` in Flyway V5 — keep new surfaces aligned from day one.

When reviewing: if **any** layer would confuse a plant PM relative to the others, **stop and align before merge** — do not “fix later.”

